 "check": {
  "describe": "Five distinct 48 dp icons in equal columns, each labelled: an amber sun with eight rays, a grey cloud centred in its square, a cloud over three slanted blue drops, a cloud over three blue dots, and a cloud over an amber bolt; below, a 32 dp storm icon. In mono the sun is a ring with rays and the clouds are white outlines. The columns are weighted: at 260 dp they get closer, at 480 dp they spread out; the icons keep their size. Below: two 96 dp morph icons (flat on the background, rich on a blue sky tile, an outlined drawing in mono) showing the sun; tapping the first steps @wx (sun -> cloud -> rain -> snow -> storm), and both morph to it: mid-morph the disc swells into the cloud outline.",
